   "source": [
    "# JAX LightGlue & SuperPoint Inference Demo
",
    "This notebook demonstrates high-performance feature matching using native JAX/Flax implementations of SuperPoint and LightGlue."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Setup & Dependencies
",
    "First, we install the necessary libraries and set up the JAX environment."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "!pip install -q jax[tpu] -f https://storage.googleapis.com/jax-releases/libtpu_releases.html
",
    "!pip install -q flax opencv-python matplotlib tqdm"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Model Implementations
",
    "We define the SuperPoint and LightGlue architectures in JAX/Flax. These implementations are designed for JIT compilation and hardware acceleration."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# In a real environment, we'd import these from our package
",
    "# from lightglue_jax.models.superpoint import SuperPoint
",
    "# from lightglue_jax.models.lightglue import LightGlue
",
    "
",
    "# For this notebook, we'll assume the 'superpoint-jax' repo is cloned
",
    "!git clone https://github.com/1kaiser/superpoint-jax.git
",
    "import sys
",
    "sys.path.append('/content/superpoint-jax')
",
    "
",
    "from lightglue_jax.models.superpoint import SuperPoint
",
    "from lightglue_jax.models.lightglue import LightGlue"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Data & Weights
",
    "We download the converted JAX weights and the test dataset."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# @title Download Weights
",
    "!mkdir -p weights
",
    "!wget -q https://github.com/1kaiser/d_jax/releases/download/v1.0.0/superpoint.msgpack -O weights/superpoint.msgpack
",
    "!wget -q https://github.com/1kaiser/d_jax/releases/download/v1.0.0/superpoint_lightglue.msgpack -O weights/superpoint_lightglue.msgpack
",
    "
",
    "# @title Download Dataset
",
    "!wget -q https://github.com/1kaiser/Media-Segment-Depth-MLP/releases/download/v0.2/input_depthMaps.zip
",
    "!unzip -q input_depthMaps.zip -d data/"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Inference Pipeline
",
    "We implement the full matching pipeline, including JIT compilation of the models."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import jax
",
    "import jax.numpy as jnp
",
    "from flax import serialization
",
    "import cv2
",
    "import numpy as np
",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt
",
    "
",
    "def load_and_preprocess(path):
",
    "    img = cv2.imread(path)
",
    "    img_rgb = cv2.cvtColor(img, cv2.COLOR_BGR2RGB)
",
    "    img_gray = cv2.cvtColor(img, cv2.COLOR_BGR2GRAY)
",
    "    img_gray = cv2.resize(img_gray, (1024, 1024))
",
    "    return img_rgb, jnp.array(img_gray[None, ..., None] / 255.0)
",
    "
",
    "# Load Weights
",
    "with open("weights/superpoint.msgpack", "rb") as f:
",
    "    sp_vars = serialization.from_bytes(None, f.read())
",
    "with open("weights/superpoint_lightglue.msgpack", "rb") as f:
",
    "    lg_vars = serialization.from_bytes(None, f.read())
",
    "
",
    "sp_model = SuperPoint()
",
    "lg_model = LightGlue(n_layers=9)
",
    "
",
    "jit_sp = jax.jit(sp_model.apply)
",
    "jit_lg = jax.jit(lg_model.apply)
",
    "
",
    "def match_frames(path0, path1):
",
    "    rgb0, inp0 = load_and_preprocess(path0)
",
    "    rgb1, inp1 = load_and_preprocess(path1)
",
    "    
",
    "    # Extract Features
",
    "    out0 = jit_sp(sp_vars, inp0)
",
    "    out1 = jit_sp(sp_vars, inp1)
",
    "    
",
    "    # Simple top-K selection logic (as in our scripts)
",
    "    def get_top_k(out, k=1024):
",
    "        scores = out['scores'][0]
",
    "        desc = out['descriptors'][0]
",
    "        indices = jnp.where(scores > 0.005)
",
    "        y, x = indices
",
    "        valid_scores = scores[indices]
",
    "        top_k = jnp.argsort(valid_scores)[::-1][:k]
",
    "        y, x = y[top_k], x[top_k]
",
    "        kpts = jnp.stack([x, y], axis=-1).astype(jnp.float32)
",
    "        iy, ix = (y/8).astype(jnp.int32), (x/8).astype(jnp.int32)
",
    "        return kpts, desc[iy, ix, :]
",
    "
",
    "    kpts0, d0 = get_top_k(out0)
",
    "    kpts1, d1 = get_top_k(out1)
",
    "    
",
    "    # Match
",
    "    lg_out = jit_lg(lg_vars, {
",
    "        "image0": {"keypoints": kpts0[None], "descriptors": d0[None]},
",
    "        "image1": {"keypoints": kpts1[None], "descriptors": d1[None]}
",
    "    })
",
    "    
",
    "    return rgb0, rgb1, kpts0, kpts1, lg_out"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Execution & Visualization
",
    "We run the inference on a pair of frames from the new dataset and visualize the results."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "frame0 = "data/input_frames/frame_0000.png"
",
    "frame1 = "data/input_frames/frame_0001.png"
",
    "
",
    "rgb0, rgb1, kpts0, kpts1, lg_out = match_frames(frame0, frame1)
",
    "
",
    "log_scores = lg_out['scores'][0, :-1, :-1]
",
    "m0 = jnp.argmax(log_scores, axis=1)
",
    "m1 = jnp.argmax(log_scores, axis=0)
",
    "mutual = (jnp.arange(len(m0)) == m1[m0])
",
    "valid = mutual & (jnp.exp(jnp.max(log_scores, axis=1)) > 0.1)
",
    "idx0 = jnp.where(valid)[0]
",
    "idx1 = m0[idx0]
",
    "
",
    "print(f"Found {len(idx0)} mutual matches.")
",
    "
",
    "# Visualization
",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(20, 10))
",
    "combined = np.hstack([cv2.resize(rgb0, (1024, 1024)), cv2.resize(rgb1, (1024, 1024))])
",
    "plt.imshow(combined)
",
    "for i0, i1 in zip(idx0, idx1):
",
    "    plt.plot([kpts0[i0, 0], kpts1[i1, 0] + 1024], [kpts0[i0, 1], kpts1[i1, 1]], 'c-', alpha=0.5)
",
    "plt.axis('off')
",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  }
 ],
